  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** SoundThinking’s core demand narrative persists, anchored in public safety technology, but deal velocity has decelerated. Large contract signings and international expansion are taking longer to materialize, while a high-profile customer loss (Chicago) underscores churn risk. Cautious optimism around product traction is countered by go-to-market friction and a broader backdrop of software sector headwinds from AI disruption concerns, which have heightened scrutiny on growth trajectories. The reset in analyst price targets reflects a market adjusting to this slower, more uncertain deployment cadence.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has reset forward guidance and valuation expectations downward, signaling a more tempered outlook on near-term revenue growth. The tone from the Q4 2025 call acknowledges attrition while targeting net new recurring revenue, revealing a balancing act between rebuilding the pipeline and managing credibility. Institutional confidence has wavered, as evidenced by Conestoga Capital Advisors exiting its position, citing a fading growth outlook. Management’s ability to convert a still-intact long-term story into timely execution remains the central question.",
